'''Djadjawurrung''' (also '''Jaara''', '''Ngurai-illam-wurrung''') is an [[Aboriginal Australian language]] spoken by the [[Dja Dja Wurrung people]] of the [[Kulin Nation|Kulin]] nation of central [[Victoria (Australia)|Victoria]]. Djadjawurrung was spoken by 16 clans around [[Murchison, Victoria|Murchison]], the central highlands region, east to Tylden, west to the Pyrenees, north to Boort and south to the [[Great Dividing Range]]. It is now extinct.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Anonymous |date=2019-07-26 |title=S31.1: Dja Dja Wurrung |url=https://collection.aiatsis.gov.au/austlang/language/s31_1 |access-date=2024-01-17 |website=collection.aiatsis.gov.au |language=en}}</ref>

